A.append(mx_app("Guanajuato", CH, 21.15, -100.88, "Guanajuato's vineyards lie around Dolores Hidalgo and San Miguel de Allende at about 1,900 to 2,100 m. Father Miguel Hidalgo taught his parishioners at Dolores to grow vines before the 1810 War of Independence, and the viceroyalty had them destroyed; the area's modern wine revival began in the 2000s with Cuna de Tierra and now includes estates around San Miguel such as Dos Búhos and San Lucas.", "Cabernet Sauvignon, Syrah, Merlot, Cabernet Franc, Tempranillo, Malbec, Sauvignon Blanc", ["Cuna de Tierra", "Dos Búhos", "Viñedo San Lucas", "Tres Raíces"]))
